# Enforcement and acceptance contract

Use for implementing or auditing integration, not as proof it already exists.
No universal script names, framework, task service, schema, platform completion
hook or dependency on another named skill is required.

## Host discovery and authorized integration

Inspect actual provisioning inputs/output, transactional reservations, plan
rendering, classification metadata, revision/seal rules, amendments, plan guards,
bound runner dispatch, tier workloads and task-record handoff. Locate every
supported caller and its ordering, including wrappers and CI if in scope.

Use one consistent validation decision or tested equivalent across entry points.
Evaluate candidate amendments before committing them; validate the admitted sealed
revision before execution dispatch. Validation must not start workload commands,
write test stubs, mutate plans, consume a different binding or silently rewrite
history. A rejected candidate may have transaction/audit effects required by the
existing provisioner; preserve those records honestly.

Separate structure from meaning: structured metadata needs an inspectable
scope-based rationale, not an arbitrary `required:false` escape. Do not classify
by substring searches over an entire document. Quoted examples, negations, test
titles and unrelated exclusion language must not override a material change.
The accountable agent reviews actual scope. Conflicting scope/declaration evidence
must fail current admission with actionable diagnostics. Do not market human
review or heuristic warnings as automated semantic proof.

Support normal, N/A, self-satisfying, deferral and excluded paths with their proper
input shapes. Validate current declarations on provisioning/publication, amendment,
explicit plan validation and supported bound execution. Exactly one declaration
is required for qualifying plans; excluded work may omit it under the host format.
Present declarations must be valid even if metadata says not-applicable.

Use actual existing revision/cutover records to distinguish historical from new
plans. Do not infer history from mtime, missing fields or a caller's self-reported
version. Preserve known historical contracts unchanged; unknown mapping is a
specific unresolved prerequisite, not permission to rewrite or bypass them.
Support actual approved amendment paths rather than requiring new plans/IDs.
That prerequisite is local to work depending on the record. Retired policy text,
archive-wide audits and original receipts are not admission requirements for
unrelated current work or gate maintenance.

The required delivery handoff enables review; it does not mandate a reviewer.
Separate read-only verification is optional unless selected by the owner or
required by an identifiable already-approved requirement. Without that selection,
do not create a review task, require independent approval or block completion.
Executor coverage assessment and required validation remain mandatory.

## Pre-implementation dispatch and amendment

Map preparation/amendment separately from read-only admission and test execution.
Provisioning and test-run checks alone do not establish pre-implementation coverage.
Locate a genuine host hook or document the Agent-first cooperative preflight.
Inspect the actual task scope, applicable contract and admitted revision. Prepare
and, where authorized, apply supported amendments before implementation starts.
Recheck current revision/identity/binding/approval at implementation dispatch using
the host's supported concurrency mechanism. A mutable native task description is
not proof that a sealed local record was updated.

If a missing declaration is discovered mid-task, pause affected implementation,
preserve evidence and safely resolve conflicting runs before amendment. Record
already-made changes and assess them under actual authorization; do not rewrite
history or turn earlier test results into proof of changed requirements.

## Acceptance cases for app enforcement

Test these through real supported entry points using isolated fixtures and
bounded supervised execution. This table is a specification, not executed proof.
For preflight denial, a workload sentinel must remain absent and sealed bytes
must remain unchanged. For failed amendment, preserve the last admitted revision,
binding and ledger history. Inspect reservation effects under actual transactions.

| Case | Required result |
|---|---|
| Material backend repair; concrete route-level recurrence and assertion | Normal declaration admitted; delivery must later supply the case |
| Frontend state repair citing only an unrelated backend test | Reject inadequate layer/coverage before publication |
| Normal declaration names a not-yet-created test file | Accept valid planned delivery; require actual case at delivery |
| Specific existing test catches the exact recurrence | Accept without redundant new test |
| Several material boundaries, only one guarded | Reject uncovered material risks |
| Missing section, duplicate fields/sections, mixed forms, placeholders | Reject current candidate; no auto-rewrite |
| N/A with supported category and concrete evidence | Accept through provisioning and amendment; residual risk tracked |
| N/A merely says "race," "no screenshot" or "hard to test" | Reject unless factual applicability and alternatives are established |
| Pure visual defect, no applicable visual automation | Permit justified N/A; do not force unrelated unit assertion |
| Entire scope is a concrete test/check for unchanged behavior | Permit genuine self-satisfaction without recursive meta-testing |
| Test-oriented title with material authorization or lifecycle change | Require normal coverage of changed behavior |
| Guard script alters admission while also adding tests | Require normal guard; no title-based self-satisfaction |
| Pure additive feature; existing behavior unchanged | Excluded from new bug-fix guard; host tests still apply |
| Cosmetic error-message edit; firing semantics unchanged | Excluded unless content itself has material privacy/contract impact |
| Actual task marked for deletion and not being implemented | No new guard demanded |
| Executing task named DELETE changes surviving behavior | Classify actual work; deletion label alone cannot exempt it |
| Non-material refactor/comment change | Excluded based on evidence, not filename |
| "Not purely additive" alongside material change | Qualifying; negation cannot trigger additive exemption |
| Unrelated exclusion in history/examples plus material scope | Qualifying; entire-document keyword escape rejected |
| Verified accepted follow-up, concrete case and approved deferral | Admit documented deferral, never claim delivered coverage |
| Follow-up merely proposed, unverifiable, cancelled or missing scope | Reject unsupported deferral; use supported resolution |
| Invalid candidate amendment | Old admitted seal, binding and history remain intact |
| Invalid current declaration at bound execution | Reject before workload sentinel or plan mutation |
| Wrong task, revision or tier context | Reject under governing admission; no workload dispatch |
| Known historical plan under its recorded older contract | Preserve and use applicable old rules; no forced syntax retrofit |
| Unknown contract mapping | Report exact prerequisite; do not relabel as historical |
| Supported task creation and every amendment form | Permitted forms round-trip without normalization into invalid forms |
| Current declaration and actual bound workload disagree | Resolve coverage/amendment; no silent workload/tier change |
| Delivered file exists but assertion misses recurrence | Executor must resolve inadequate delivery; a selected verifier also reports it |
| Valid N/A or deferral handoff | Verify evidence/disposition; no fictional automated guard result |
| Read-only verification finds a gap | Report it; no patches, runs, resealing or task completion changes |
| Complete guard delivery/validation; optional separate review not selected | No review blocker or pending required acceptance; handoff remains available |
| Separate review is an explicit owner selection or existing approved requirement | Identify that basis and apply only its actual scope; no invented approval system |
| Unresolved historical record unrelated to a current plan | Preserve record and report limitation without blocking independent current work |
| Start on an adequate admitted plan | Preflight reuses it; no gratuitous amendment or repeated approval |
| Start reveals missing guard within covered authorization | Prepare/apply supported amendment; re-admit before implementation |
| Candidate changes exceed existing authorization | Request only the uncovered decision; no implementation against the candidate |
| Native Plan edited while local seal remains old | Detect mismatch; do not treat visible text as updated admission |
| Preflight passed but plan changed before dispatch | Reject stale revision; re-establish current admission |
| Gap found after implementation starts | Pause affected work, preserve changes/evidence and amend before resuming |
| Plan amendment requested during an active validation run | Do not mutate binding under the run; use supported quiescence/cancellation |
| No genuine native Start hook exists | Document Agent-first cooperative preflight; no platform-interception claim |

## Migration boundaries

Keep existing tier workloads, baseline records, IDs, bindings, reservations,
tombstones and ledgers intact. A definition update alone does not activate new
checks in any application. Replace only explicitly authorized integration code
and instructions through supported maintenance routes; document adoption and
which new plan contract it affects. Remove validation-time automatic stub editing
only as an authorized behavior change with its own applicable guard evidence.

Distinguish package text checks, isolated enforcement fixtures, actual caller
wiring, executor delivery and separate read-only verification. A passed fixture
does not establish host activation or control Replit platform completion.
